# Codebase Refactor & Architecture Overhaul

The MathViz codebase has grown significantly, resulting in a monolithic `MathVisualizer.tsx` component that duplicates state logic and shadows other specialized component files. This plan outlines a systematic restructuring to improve developer experience and application robustness.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This refactor involves moving almost all UI components in `MathVisualizer.tsx` to separate files and changing how state is accessed. While functionality will remain identical, the file structure will change drastically.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Component Modularization
Move sub-components currently declared within `MathVisualizer.tsx` to their own files in `src/components/math-visualizer/`.

- **[NEW]** `src/components/common/KaTeX.tsx`: Centralize `KaTeXInline` and `KaTeXBlock`.
- **[NEW]** `src/components/math-visualizer/WelcomeScreen.tsx`
- **[NEW]** `src/components/math-visualizer/ShortcutsOverlay.tsx`
- **[NEW]** `src/components/math-visualizer/NavigationOverlays.tsx`: Group `LessonInfoPanel` and `StepTOCPanel`.
- **[NEW]** `src/components/math-visualizer/LessonControls.tsx`: Group `StepDots`, `SceneTabs`, `LessonProgressBar`.
- **[NEW]** `src/components/math-visualizer/NarrativeSidebar.tsx`: Extract `StepNarrative` and layout shells.

### 2. Canvas Engine Unification
The current `MathCanvas.tsx` is a simplified "orphan" file. We will replace it with the advanced rendering logic found in the internal `MathVizCanvas`.

- **[MODIFY]** [MathCanvas.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/MathCanvas.tsx): 
    - Integrate the 1000+ lines of advanced rendering logic (staggered entry, morphing, label collision avoidance) from the monolithic file.
    - Ensure it correctly subscribes to `useMathVizStore` for all coordinate and zoom state.

### 3. State Management Refinement
Shift `MathVisualizer.tsx` from local `useState` to the centralized `useMathVizStore`.

- **[MODIFY]** [store.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/lib/store.ts):
    - Ensure all required state keys (like `showShortcuts`, `showTOC`) are present or managed consistently.
- **[MODIFY]** [MathVisualizer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/MathVisualizer.tsx):
    - Remove ~1500 lines of component definitions and local state.
    - Transform into a lean container component that composes the new modular parts.

### 4. Cleanup & Utilities
- **[MODIFY]** `src/lib/utils.ts`: Move pure helpers like `flattenSteps`, `totalSteps`, `totalElements`.
- **[DELETE]** Remove any unused "v1" component files that were rendered obsolete by the new modular structure.

---

## Open Questions

- **Transition Animations**: Should we keep the current `Framer Motion` usage for UI overlays, or move toward standard CSS transitions for performance and simplicity during the refactor?
- **Store Persistence**: Currently, only a few fields are persisted. Should we persist the `currentStepIndex` so users can resume their progress after a refresh?

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run build` to ensure no broken imports or type errors.
- Use the browser subagent to verify that navigation, playback, and canvas morphing still function correctly.

### Manual Verification
- Verify that keyboard shortcuts still trigger the correct panels.
- Check that "Lesson Picker" favorites and recents are preserved across state changes.
